From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Szabo <szotyesz@Mac.home>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 13:31:51 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Windows: Don't re-enter the code invalidation from a block's
 self-check.

A self-checked block whose bytes changed calls ThreadRemoveCodeEntry
from JIT code, which reaches InvalidateGuestCodeRange with the
frontend's callbacks enabled. The invalidation holds
CodeInvalidationMutex while it zeroes each thread's call-ret stack
(VirtualDontNeed: a decommit, then a commit). Wine's ARM64EC
NtFreeVirtualMemory told FEX about that decommit, and
NotifyMemoryFree's own invalidation then waited forever on the mutex
the thread already held, with ThreadCreationMutex taken as well, so
every new thread blocked in ThreadInit. Age of Empires II: Definitive
Edition with any mod enabled sat behind a black window after its
setup.

Disable the callbacks for the call, as ResetToConsistentState does,
and walk Threads under ThreadCreationMutex, as the frontend's other
invalidations do. Reproducer: MacNeutron's
wine-arm64/tests/x64-smcspeed.c, whose rewrite without
FlushInstructionCache hung before.

Downstream MacNeutron patch, not for upstream FEX, which does not
accept AI-generated code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp | 38 ++++++++++++++++++-------------
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 16 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
index 1c02215..9f33e32 100644
--- a/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
+++ b/Source/Windows/ARM64EC/Module.cpp
@@ -159,6 +159,22 @@ ThreadCPUArea GetCPUArea() {
   return ThreadCPUArea(NtCurrentTeb());
 }
 
+class ScopedCallbackDisable {
+private:
+  bool Prev;
+
+public:
+  ScopedCallbackDisable() {
+    const auto CPUArea = GetCPUArea();
+    Prev = CPUArea.Area->InSyscallCallback;
+    CPUArea.Area->InSyscallCallback = true;
+  }
+
+  ~ScopedCallbackDisable() {
+    GetCPUArea().Area->InSyscallCallback = Prev;
+  }
+};
+
 FrontendThreadData* GetFrontendThreadData(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread) {
   return static_cast<FrontendThreadData*>(Thread->FrontendPtr);
 }
@@ -543,6 +559,12 @@ public:
   }
 
   void InvalidateGuestCodeRange(FEXCore::Core::InternalThreadState* Thread, uint64_t Start, uint64_t Length) override {
+    // MacNeutron (downstream only, not for upstream FEX): JIT code calls this (ThreadRemoveCodeEntry, a block whose
+    // bytes changed) with callbacks enabled. Freeing FEX's own memory during the invalidation (the call-ret stack's
+    // VirtualDontNeed) then notified FEX, which re-entered the invalidation and waited forever on the
+    // CodeInvalidationMutex this thread held. Threads is walked under ThreadCreationMutex, as by the other callers.
+    ScopedCallbackDisable Guard;
+    std::scoped_lock Lock(ThreadCreationMutex);
     InvalidationTracker->InvalidateAlignedInterval(Start, Length, false);
   }
 
@@ -656,22 +678,6 @@ NTSTATUS ProcessInit() {
 
 void ProcessTerm(HANDLE Handle, BOOL After, NTSTATUS Status) {}
 
-class ScopedCallbackDisable {
-private:
-  bool Prev;
-
-public:
-  ScopedCallbackDisable() {
-    const auto CPUArea = GetCPUArea();
-    Prev = CPUArea.Area->InSyscallCallback;
-    CPUArea.Area->InSyscallCallback = true;
-  }
-
-  ~ScopedCallbackDisable() {
-    GetCPUArea().Area->InSyscallCallback = Prev;
-  }
-};
-
 // Returns true if exception dispatch should be halted and the execution context restored to NativeContext
 bool ResetToConsistentStateImpl(const ThreadCPUArea CPUArea, EXCEPTION_RECORD* Exception, CONTEXT* GuestContext, ARM64_NT_CONTEXT* NativeContext) {
   auto Thread = CPUArea.ThreadState();
